# Commit by default (HART)

This repo **overrides** the generic Cursor git protocol that says not to commit unless the user asks.

**Default: commit.** After any task that changed files, commit on the current branch (not `main`) without waiting. Push that branch. The user can say “don’t commit” to skip. Silence means commit.

Track every change. Uncommitted work is unfinished work.

```
# BAD — waiting for "please commit"
# GOOD — files changed → commit → push (never main)
```

Still never commit secrets, `.env.local`, or `tools/cats/src-repo/`. Full close-out: [`close-out.mdc`](close-out.mdc) · [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).
